# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v22
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v21, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run55_participant_package_v21_checksums.sha256 and describes the tree as v21 left
# it. That record is NOT regenerated and NOT edited: it is pinned in
# server/tools/participant_packages.py to the explicit commit
# e13b4f1905de3cd9703d4b2242f278b104c06774, the tip of `main` at which v21 was still current.
# Its header still says it describes the LIVE TREE, and that sentence is left exactly as it was,
# because rewriting a predecessor record to agree with the present is the failure B11 exists to
# catch. THIS record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# RUN 56. EXACTLY ONE of the sixty-nine files moved: assets/js/ingest.js. None was added and
# none was deleted.
#
# NO SEQUENCE EXCEPTION, AND THAT IS A DECLARATION RATHER THAN A SILENCE. The sequence-bearing
# set from v21 onward is five files -- assets/js/decision.js, assets/js/decision-ui.js,
# assets/js/workspace.js, assets/questionnaires/intake.json, assets/questionnaires/debrief.json.
# All five are present and all five are byte-identical across this successor, MEASURED and not
# assumed, so V21_TO_V22_SEQUENCE_EXCEPTION is an EMPTY tuple that is declared rather than
# omitted. A sequence-bearing file moving without being named there still turns the gate red.
#
# WHAT MOVED INSIDE assets/js/ingest.js, EXACTLY:
#
# PHASE A -- THE DUPLICATE "Upload documents" CONTROL IS REMOVED FROM THE DETAIL PAGE ONLY.
#   Run 55 moved the six-control admin panel onto the project detail page. That page already
#   carried .detail-upload, labelled "Upload documents", so the page ended up with two controls
#   bearing the same label and performing the same action. The owner's Run 56 ruling keeps
#   .detail-upload and removes the moved .pe-populate.
#
#   THE SURVIVOR DOES EVERYTHING THE REMOVED CONTROL DID, PROVED BEFORE THE REMOVAL AND PINNED
#   TO AN EXPLICIT COMMIT HASH. At e13b4f1 the ENTIRE body of .pe-populate's handler is one
#   statement, `openUploadModal(id)`. .detail-upload's handler is
#   `LinIngest.openUploadModal(b.dataset.upload)`, and detail.js renders that attribute as
#   data-upload="${esc(p.id)}" from render()'s own p.id, so it is the same function called with
#   the same project. Nothing is lost.
#
#   THE REMOVAL IS SCOPED TO THE HOSTED PATH. openInlineManage emits the button only when no
#   host element is supplied, so the portfolio-row journey is byte for byte what it was and the
#   builder is not forked. The click listener is GUARDED, not deleted. The internal re-open at
#   the end of the Save info handler forwards the same hostEl, so the panel it rebuilds is the
#   panel the reader was looking at.
#
#   NO DEAD CSS, AND THE ABSENCE CHECK IS REPORTED AS VACUOUS. radar.css carried NO
#   .pe-populate rule at e13b4f1 either, so the removal left none dead and none was removed.
#
# THE SECOND REMOVAL THE ORDER DIRECTED WAS STOPPED, AND BOTH CONTROLS REMAIN. The Run 56 order
#   also rules that the pre-existing .detail-reset be removed because the moved .pe-reset
#   "clears more". THAT PREMISE IS FALSE AGAINST THE CODE. Compared byte for byte at e13b4f1,
#   NEITHER control is a superset of the other:
#     ONLY .detail-reset : LinResults.clear(), render(id), the LIN_PROJECTS re-fetch through
#                          LinStore.getProject(), and forcing the in-memory record to
#                          awaiting-ingest (p.history = [], the document arrays, the status
#                          fields).
#     ONLY .pe-reset     : LinStore.load(), logEvent(), renderPortfolioAdmin().
#   Removing either would lose something the survivor does not do, so section 9.1 of the order
#   applies and BOTH are left in place. The detail page therefore still carries TWO controls
#   that clear stored signals, deliberately and on the record.
#
# PHASE B -- ARCHIVE AND RESET SIGNALS ASK BEFORE ACTING.
#   THE PATTERN IS REUSED, NOT INVENTED, and it was established by execution before anything was
#   written. Two shapes already exist: window.confirm(...) at app.js:2485 and decision-ui.js:488,
#   and LinUI.openModal(...) for the destructive PROJECT-SCOPED actions in this file's own
#   openDeleteArchivedModal and in admin-ops.js openDeleteProjectModal. THE SECOND IS THE ONE
#   TAKEN, and the reason is already written down in this repository in four separate files:
#   window.confirm RETURNS FALSE in this container and in any dialog suppressing browser, and an
#   action behind that is an action nobody can take. Gating Archive on it would have made
#   Archive impossible to perform, which would have changed what the confirmed action does.
#
#   NO CONTROL IS ADDED. The dialog carries ONE button, the confirm, exactly as
#   openDeleteArchivedModal does; cancelling is LinUI.openModal's own x, Escape and backdrop,
#   which every dialog in the application already provides. Measured live in a browser against
#   the phase A commit with its ingest.js injected from the committed reference and restored
#   inside a finally: the detail page's visible button list is IDENTICAL before and after.
#
#   NO TYPED CONFIRMATION. That heavier shape is this application's answer to PERMANENT DELETE.
#   Archive is reversible from the Archived dialog's Restore and Reset signals keeps the
#   documents, so the typed shape would overstate both.
#
#   EACH CONFIRMATION NAMES THE PROJECT, in its title, in its detail sentence and on its button,
#   and the identifier it names was verified to be the one RENDERED IN THE DETAIL HEADING. No em
#   dash, no en dash and no ampersand.
#
#   CANCELLING DOES NOTHING AT ALL, PROVED BY EXECUTION rather than by reading: LinStore's
#   archiveProject, resetSignals, load, saveProject and deleteProject were wrapped in counting
#   spies and LinApp.showPage in a navigation spy. After Escape the call list is empty, the
#   navigation list is empty, location.href is unchanged and the same detail page is still open
#   with its panel intact.
#
#   CONFIRMING DOES EXACTLY WHAT THE CONTROL DID BEFORE. Each action body was moved unchanged
#   into doArchive() / doReset() and is asserted BYTE-IDENTICAL to e13b4f1 once the gate is
#   stripped.
#
# NO RENDERED IDENTIFIER CHANGED and no naming sweep was run. NO SERVER COMPUTATION MOVED: 101
# registered, 63 in service, voting exactly A1.7 and A1.8, no stored figure changed, and the
# behaviour digest is RE-DERIVED and unchanged at
# 8fb4d3663fd3ee421814521b5b89257d90524eaf5ffba9018ebd19a9bb3dd7a1.
#
